# function pick(value) { if (value is a Shape) value.side; else value.side }  pick(circle); pick(square); pick(label)    function choose(value) { the same }  choose(circle); choose(somethingNoTableLists)    spare.side
# The parameter of the first function gets more layouts than the analysis follows in one set, so it holds the untracked object. That of the second holds the unknown object.
# A test has run in front of the arm that is taken, so whatever arrives there lies inside the tested type: an object of another layout is cut, primitives are cut, and neither placeholder passes as itself.
# Whatever a placeholder stood for has passed the test, so it is an object of the family, and one that the placeholder covers: of the untracked object the circle and the square that the analysis
# has stopped following, of the unknown object what has escaped, which is nothing here. The circle that is never passed fits the type and takes nobody's place.
# The arm that is not taken leaves out only what is sure to pass the test, so there each placeholder is still what it was
# OPTIONS: limit=MaxValueFlowSetMembers:2
# STATISTIC: MaxValueFlowSetMembersHits >= 1
# RUN: valueflow-families receivers
# CHECK: application accesses 6 unknown-object 1 object-without-layout 1 several-layouts 1 one-layout 2 no-object 0 untracked-object 1
# RUN(VALUES): valueflow-why values=f0:v5 values=f0:v6 values=f0:v13 values=f1:v3 values=f1:v5 values=f2:v3 values=f2:v5
# VALUES: values=f0:v5
# VALUES: operand 2 1 members: [[circle]]@f0
# VALUES: values=f0:v6
# VALUES: operand 2 1 members: [[square]]@f0
# VALUES: values=f0:v13
# VALUES: operand 0 1 members: [[spare]]@f0
# VALUES: values=f1:v3
# VALUES: operand 0
# VALUES-NOT: unknown
# VALUES-NOT: untracked
# VALUES-NOT: [[spare]]@f0
# VALUES: 2 members: [[circle]]@f0 [[square]]@f0
# VALUES: values=f1:v5
# VALUES: operand 0 {{*}} untracked
# VALUES-NOT: [[spare]]@f0
# VALUES: values=f2:v3
# VALUES: operand 0
# VALUES-NOT: primitive
# VALUES-NOT: unknown
# VALUES-NOT: untracked
# VALUES-NOT: [[spare]]@f0
# VALUES: 1 members: [[circle]]@f0
# VALUES: values=f2:v5
# VALUES: operand 0 {{*}} unknown
# VALUES-NOT: [[spare]]@f0

module m0 path="main.js" displayPath="main.js" body=f0
entry module=m0
layout L0 name="Shape"
layout L1 name="Circle" supertypes=[L0]
layout L2 name="Square" supertypes=[L0]
layout L3 name="Label"
function f0 name="main" module=m0 kind=Module results=[{type=anything}] {
    v0 = NewObject layout=L1 fields=[]
    v1 = NewObject layout=L2 fields=[]
    v2 = NewObject layout=L3 fields=[]
    v3 = NewObject layout=L1 fields=[]
    v4 = NewClosure function=f1
    v5 = Call v4, -, v0
    v6 = Call v4, -, v1
    v7 = Call v4, -, v2
    v8 = Builtin builtin=GlobalThis
    v9 = PropGet v8 key="somethingThatNoTableLists" [isFreeName]
    v10 = NewClosure function=f2
    v11 = Call v10, -, v0
    v12 = Call v10, -, v9
    v13 = PropGet v3 key="side"
    Return
}
function f1 name="pick" module=m0 parameters=[{type=anything}] results=[{type=anything}] {
    v1 = TypeTest v0 testedType=L0
    Branch v1 -> taken b1(| 0), notTaken b2(| 0)
  b1(v2):
    v3 = PropGet v2 key="side"
    Return
  b2(v4):
    v5 = PropGet v4 key="side"
    Return
}
function f2 name="choose" module=m0 parameters=[{type=anything}] results=[{type=anything}] {
    v1 = TypeTest v0 testedType=L0
    Branch v1 -> taken b1(| 0), notTaken b2(| 0)
  b1(v2):
    v3 = PropGet v2 key="side"
    Return
  b2(v4):
    v5 = PropGet v4 key="side"
    Return
}
